  "generated_text": "First, multiply the numerator and the denominator by the complex conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[\n\\frac{2+2i}{-3+4i} \\cdot \\frac{-3-4i}{-3-4i}\n\\]\n\nNext, expand the numerator and the denominator:\n\\[\n\\text{umerator:} \\quad (2+2i)(-3-4i) = -6 - 8i + 6i - 8i^2 = -6 - 14i + 8 = -14i\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Denominator:} \\quad (-3+4i)(-3-4i) = 9 + 12i - 12i - 16i^2 = 9 + 6 = 25\n\\]\n\nNow, divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\\[\n\\frac{-14i}{25} = \\frac{-14i}{25} = -\\frac{14}{25}i = -\\frac{2}{5}i\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified form is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{2}{5}i}\n\\]",
